# Verify the app compiles

`vitest` only runs `tests/`. It will not parse `src/components`, `src/app`, or other TSX.
A stray `)}` can pass every unit test and fail Vercel on `next build`.

After changing `.tsx`, `.ts` under `src/app` or `src/components`, or CSS imported by the app:

1. Run `npm run lint` before you treat the work as done.
2. If the change is deploy-sensitive (layout, JSX wrappers, next config), also run `npm run build`.
3. Do not rely on `npm test` alone as a pipeline check.

A syntax error in JSX is a failed compile, not a failed test.
